---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Container from '../components/primitives/Container.astro';
import Heading from '../components/primitives/Heading.astro';
import Section from '../components/primitives/Section.astro';
import Text from '../components/primitives/Text.astro';

const meta = {
  title: 'Privacy Policy',
  description: 'Privacy policy for Splendid Wren Marketing.',
  canonicalPath: '/privacy',
};
---

<BaseLayout meta={meta}>
  <Section tone="white">
    <Container class="max-w-4xl">
      <Heading level={1}>Privacy Policy</Heading>
      <Text class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-brand-700">
        Updated 22 October 2026
      </Text>

      <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-base leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
        <section>
          <Heading level={2} class="text-2xl">Introduction</Heading>
          <div class="mt-3 space-y-4">
            <p>
              At Splendid Wren Marketing, we want to be upfront about how we handle your information. This policy
              explains what personal information we collect through our website, why we collect it, how we use it,
              and the choices you have.
            </p>
            <p>
              We are committed to handling personal information in line with the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and the
              Australian Privacy Principles (APPs).
            </p>
            <p>
              By using our website or engaging our services, you agree to the practices described in this policy. If
              you have any questions, you are welcome to get in touch through the details at the bottom of this page.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section>
          <Heading level={2} class="text-2xl">What personal information we collect</Heading>
          <p class="mt-3">Depending on how you interact with us, we may collect:</p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 pl-5">
            <li class="list-disc">
              <strong>Contact form submissions:</strong> When you fill in an enquiry or contact form on our site, we
              collect information such as your name, email address, phone number, business name, and whatever details
              you share in your message.
            </li>
            <li class="list-disc">
              <strong>Newsletter opt-ins:</strong> If you subscribe to our mailing list, we collect your email
              address and, if provided, your name.
            </li>
            <li class="list-disc">
              <strong>Client and lead information:</strong> Once you engage with our services, we may store your
              contact and business details, along with notes on our conversations and the services we provide, in our
              customer relationship management (CRM) system.
            </li>
            <li class="list-disc">
              <strong>Website usage data:</strong> We use cookies and analytics tools to understand how visitors use
              our site - things like pages viewed, time spent on site, device and browser type, and general location
              at a country or city level. This is aggregated, non-identifying information wherever possible.
            </li>

          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4">
            We do not knowingly collect sensitive information, such as health, financial, or government-identifier
            details, through our website, and we ask that you do not include this kind of information in any form you
            submit to us.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <Heading level={2} class="text-2xl">How we collect personal information</Heading>
          <p class="mt-3">We collect personal information:</p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 pl-5">
            <li class="list-disc">
              Directly from you, when you fill in a form, subscribe to our newsletter, email us, or otherwise get in touch;
            </li>
            <li class="list-disc">
              Automatically, through cookies and analytics tools when you browse our website; and
            </li>
            <li class="list-disc">
              Through our business tools, such as our CRM, once a working relationship begins.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <Heading level={2} class="text-2xl">Why we collect, hold, and use your information</Heading>
          <p class="mt-3">We use personal information to:</p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 pl-5">
            <li class="list-disc">Respond to your enquiries and provide the services you have asked for;</li>
            <li class="list-disc">
              Manage our relationship with you as a lead or client, including invoicing and account administration;
            </li>
            <li class="list-disc">Send you our newsletter or marketing communications, where you have opted in;</li>
            <li class="list-disc">Understand how people use our website, so we can improve it; and</li>
            <li class="list-disc">Meet our legal and regulatory obligations.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-4">
            We do not sell your personal information, and we only use it for the purposes described here, or a purpose
            you would reasonably expect.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <Heading level={2} class="text-2xl">Website services and analytics choices</Heading>
          <div class="mt-3 space-y-4">
            <p>Vercel hosts this website and processes requests to its pages and contact endpoint. The site loads fonts from Google Fonts. Hosting and font requests provide those services with network information such as your IP address.</p>
            <p>Our contact endpoint sends your enquiry fields to our configured email recipient through SMTP2GO. Enquiry text, names and email addresses are not included in our analytics events. Operational logs record outcomes and error codes, without the enquiry text.</p>
            <p>Optional measurement starts only after you accept analytics. This includes Google Analytics, Vercel Web Analytics and, when enabled, Vercel Speed Insights. Before a choice or after declining, these measurement tools are not loaded. The contact endpoint also requires an explicit analytics consent value before sending a server completion event to Google.</p>
            <p>We store your analytics choice in your browser. Use <button type="button" data-analytics-preferences class="cursor-pointer font-semibold underline underline-offset-4">Analytics preferences</button> to change it. Declining optional analytics does not prevent enquiries. Forms submitted without JavaScript do not opt into analytics.</p>
            <p>Measurement includes page paths, broad interaction categories, external brand-audit clicks and accepted contact submissions. Query strings are removed from page locations sent by our measurement code. Clicking the brand-audit link opens a separate HubSpot-hosted site; a click does not confirm that you completed its form. That site controls its own forms and consent choices.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section>
          <Heading level={2} class="text-2xl">Sharing your information</Heading>
          <p class="mt-3">We do not share your personal information with third parties except:</p>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 pl-5">
            <li class="list-disc">
              With the website service providers described above when needed to deliver those services;
            </li>
            <li class="list-disc">Where we are required to by law; or</li>
            <li class="list-disc">With your consent.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="mt-4 space-y-4">
            <p>
              Service providers also publish their own privacy policies. The website configuration alone does not establish their storage locations or retention periods.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>Processing locations:</strong> The Vercel function serving our contact form is currently configured in the United States. We have not verified an Australia-only storage or processing commitment for our website and email services.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section>
          <Heading level={2} class="text-2xl">Direct marketing</Heading>
          <div class="mt-3 space-y-4">
            <p>
              If you have subscribed to our newsletter or opted in to marketing communications, we may send you
              updates, offers, and content by email. Every marketing email includes an unsubscribe link, and you can
              opt out at any time.
            </p>
            <p>
              Even after you unsubscribe from marketing, we may still need to contact you about services you have
              engaged us for.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section>
          <Heading level={2} class="text-2xl">How we store and protect your information</Heading>
          <div class="mt-3 space-y-4">
            <p>
              We take reasonable steps to protect the personal information we hold from misuse, interference, loss,
              and unauthorised access, modification, or disclosure. Our website uses encrypted HTTPS connections. Access to contact information is limited to people who need it to respond to enquiries.
            </p>
            <p>
              No method of storage or transmission over the internet is completely secure, so while we do our best to
              protect your information, we cannot guarantee absolute security.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section>
          <Heading level={2} class="text-2xl">Access, correction, and complaints</Heading>
          <div class="mt-3 space-y-4">
            <p>
              You have the right to ask us what personal information we hold about you, and to request that we correct
              it if it is inaccurate or out of date. You can also ask us to delete your information or unsubscribe from
              our communications at any time.
            </p>
            <p>To make a request, contact us using the details below. We will respond within a reasonable timeframe.</p>
            <p>
              If you are not satisfied with how we have handled your personal information, you can lodge a complaint
              with us directly, or contact the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC):
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5">
              <li class="list-disc">
                Website:
                <a
                  href="https://www.oaic.gov.au"
                  class="font-semibold text-brand-800 underline decoration-brand-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-950"
                  rel="noreferrer"
                >
                  www.oaic.gov.au
                </a>
              </li>
              <li class="list-disc">
                Phone: <a href="tel:1300363992" class="font-semibold text-brand-800">1300 363 992</a>
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section>
          <Heading level={2} class="text-2xl">Changes to this policy</Heading>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We may update this policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or legal obligations. We
            will post the updated version on this page with a new last updated date. We encourage you to check back
            periodically.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <Heading level={2} class="text-2xl">Contact us</Heading>
          <p class="mt-3">
            If you have any questions about this privacy policy or how we handle your personal information, please get
            in touch:
          </p>
          <p class="mt-4">
            <strong>Splendid Wren Marketing</strong><br />
            Email:
            <a
              href="mailto:hello@splendidwrenmarketing.com.au"
              class="font-semibold text-brand-800 underline decoration-brand-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-brand-950"
            >
              hello@splendidwrenmarketing.com.au
            </a>
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
